  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/44740f82eec4457d2772aee7e292f1ab5f908723487a7f195a86a356ea5af810.png)\n\nIndeed, we have that $g(x)$ is continuous on the open interval $(-3,1).$ \n\nAdditionally, the function is left-continuous at $x=1.$ Hence, it is continuous on the interval $(-3,1].$\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x)$ is not left-continuous at $x=1.$\n\n- $h(x)$, $p(x)$, and $q(x)$ are not continuous at some point that lies inside the interval $(-3,1].$",
